A||||6||Fierochic88||86 2m4 Clutch Problems - Need Advice||||5||
Z||000000||Fierochic88||06-10-2001||09:10 PM||||Hey Everyone -<BR>    I need a little advice on my 86 Coupe.  I paid $50 for it a year ago and boy was it a deal (but that's a story for another day).  Anyways, at that point it needed a new clutch which it recieved a few months ago, along with a new pressure  plate and all the other goodies.  Initially the gas pedal bogged and my dad and I replaced the throttle cable and all was well.  At the same time it was hard to shift but it was overshadowed by the gas pedal.  Now that it is fixed the hard shifting problem has become more apparent.  It is intermittent though and only occurs at certain times.  I have replaced the clutch pedal (from aluminum to steel), as well as bleeding the clutch several times.  Any other ideas as what could be causing it?  It only occurs about every 3 or 4 times it is driven.  <BR>Jennifer<BR>Silver 88 GT<BR>Silver 86 Cp<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||RAREW66||06-11-2001||12:07 AM||||This might sound stupid, but have you checked the fluid level and if so is the correct fluid in the trans?<P>The 88 Helm manual does recommend Synchro-Mesh trans fluid<P>Fred||||reg||1
Z||000002||Scott||06-11-2001||12:47 AM||||I think I can help, as I've had this problem with all my 2.5 cars. This is what I did and it helped a lot: new bushings on the transmition end of the shiftlinkage (Rodney Dickman sells a kit), lubed the shifter mech. up front (w/ teflon to avoid dust collection), adjusted the shift cables, drained the fluid from the tranny and replaced it w/ Mobil-1 20w50 (although I've heard that even 5w30 works well). This worked for me. Good luck.<BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierochic88||06-11-2001||10:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RAREW66:<BR><B>This might sound stupid, but have you checked the fluid level and if so is the correct fluid in the trans?<P>Fred</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The fluid level is okay.  Checked that when we bled it.  I honestly am not sure what it has in it right now but I know Dad picked up some more Synchro Mesh so I will update you when I get that in (hopefully tonight)<P>Jennifer<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||johnt671||06-11-2001||05:00 PM||||I had some problems with my four speed and changed to Mobil 1 5-30 oil, Valvoline synthetic brake fluid in the clutch system, and followed V-8 Archies way to bleed the system.  Mine shifts great now.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierochic88||06-11-2001||10:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>and followed V-8 Archies way to bleed the system.  Mine shifts great now.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>What way is this?<P>Jennifer<BR>Silver 88 GT<BR>Silver 86 Cp<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||RAREW66||06-12-2001||12:26 AM||||Go to V-8 Archies website and look under his Archisms section. There is a lot of useful info there.<P>Fred||||reg||1
